  "results": [
    "Interactive or headless batch cropping with a pip-installable CLI"
  ],
  "why": "A chore from the computer-vision work at Infortrend: folders of same-layout images that all needed the same region cut out. Redrawing the box on every picture only works if your hand never drifts, so the box is drawn once and replayed as numbers, in the window or from the command line.",
  "gains": "Screenshots, scans, video frames, product photos, dataset images: any folder that shares a layout gets the same crop in one pass. Names, formats, EXIF and colour profiles are kept, the originals are left alone, and a saved preset repeats the job later without a window.",
